s her whether even if trump committed  crimes  we should just move on because trump is  gone and jane mayer points out  listen it's true that lots of the  countries  that charge former leaders with crimes  are not necessarily the countries we're  trying to emulate but  she argues that if the crimes trump  committed aren't even related to the  presidency  these are business crimes for example  what reason is there not to pursue them  pursue them and this is an important  point  we know that every president makes  decisions that lead to deaths  but we don't charge presidents in those  cases because it would make being  president impossible i'm not saying  that i'm against war crimes charges  that's not at all what i'm saying but  every time you cut aid or shift military  resources  send troops into war change some welfare  program do a drone strike  every presidency leads to civilian  deaths some of which could have been  avoided right or wrong  u.s presidents don't get charged with  that stuff and we can have a debate  about that but that's not what we're  talking about here  if we find out trump was laundering  money through his business  who cares if he was president for a  four-year period  it's unrelated to him being president  and there shouldn't be a culture of  impunity as jane mayer  correctly points out the possible  financial crimes  and fraud in new york are significant  taking tax deductions on things that  aren't tax deductible to the tune of  millions of dollars  including even some of those hush money  payments that donald trump made  exaggerating or diminishing the claimed  value of real estate  to manipulate lenders and taxation  authorities to his benefit  there's a very long list here and these  are crimes in the state of new york  on the tail end of this the question of  prison comes up  are the things being investigated  theoretically punishable by prison time  yes would trump get prison time  even if found guilty it's possible  would he serve it i can't imagine jane  mayer says in the interview  she believes trump would flee the  country if he actually were  sentenced to prison time the truth is i  don't think that's very likely  but we're in such unprecedented  territory that it's very difficult to  predict  my sense is the most likely scenario is  there's no prison time  and trump doesn't have to flee i still  believe that's the most  obvious and logical scenario the  importance to me of criminally charging  trump  isn't to put him in prison it's twofold  first it's to show that a president  isn't above the law  and maybe that will prevent another  president from being as corrupt and  criminal as donald trump  maybe that's naive but that's one  important element of this  secondly as a very practical matter if  there are criminal charges against  donald trump  it could just keep him too busy to even  think about running again in 2024 and  that would be a very good thing  we'll have more coverage of this on the  david pakman show instagram  you can follow us there at david pakman  show follow me on instagram at  david.pacman if you want to see  me um uh what would be the right word  that's not really accosted  smothered by a dog that doesn't  understand the concept of personal space  follow me on instagram at david.pakman  one of our sponsors is privacy.com  they're giving you five dollars when you  sign up for  their completely free service at  privacy.com  pacman i've been using privacy for a  little over a year now you've heard me  talk about it before  it's a lifesaver and here's how it works  takes just a couple of minutes to set up  anytime you buy something online or on  the phone  instead of actually using your real  credit card number  the privacy app and the browser plug-in  let you give each company  a randomized virtual credit card number  that you create out of thin air it'll  even auto fill the card number with one  click  and the payment is taken out of your  checking account  without the merchant ever knowing your  real information so this allows you to  keep  your banking information secure but also  to take control of your finances you can  create  up to 12 of these virtual credit cards a  month you can set  spending limits you can freeze them you  can delete them anytime you want so when  you do this  it means you're not going to be charged  when you don't want to be  because you can destroy the virtual card  number  right after using it which for instance  i love using free trials because i know  i won't be charged when the trial is  over  if i use a virtual credit card number  you're keeping your identity private  by not telling companies who you are  you're keeping your bank or  credit card info protected against data  breaches and identity theft  and it's free and like i said you'll get  five dollars  to spend when you sign up at privacy.com  slash pacman
 

